<section>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    Using <i>m</i>₁ = 2 kg, <i>m</i>₂ = 3 kg, <i>P</i> = 10 N, first with
    <i>μ</i> = 0:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>The surface is smooth, so the pair moves with <i>P</i>.</li>
    <li>System: 10 = 5<i>a</i>, so <i>a</i> = 2 m/s²</li>
    <li>Trailer: <i>T</i> = 2 × 2 = 4 N</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    These match the live values at the default settings. Now take the same
    masses and force with <i>μ</i> = 0.2.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Total friction <i>F</i> = 0.2 × 5 × 9.81 = 9.81 N</li>
    <li>10 N &gt; 9.81 N, so the pair still moves.</li>
    <li>System: 10 − 9.81 = 5<i>a</i>, so <i>a</i> = 0.038 m/s²</li>
    <li><i>T</i> = 2 × 10 / 5 = 4 N — the same <i>T</i>, because both particles share <i>μ</i></li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Raise <i>μ</i> on the slider to see <i>a</i> fall while <i>T</i> holds.
    If <i>F</i> reaches <i>P</i>, the status becomes AT REST.
  </p>
</section>
